    "reason": "Over Sep 1-30 this campaign spent $1,500 and earned $6,000 in revenue, a ROAS of 4.0 on 60 conversions ($25 CPA). Results were flat every day, and its ROAS is more than double example-b's. It is stable, so a moderate increase of about 20% (from its actual $50/day spend to $60) is low risk and unlikely to reset learning. Caveat: the 100 budget is shared with example-b, and a shared budget can't be set per campaign. To apply this, move it to its own $60 budget, which keeps the account total at $100/day. If you keep the shared budget, leave it at 100 and don't expect a reallocation. Also, the data ends Sep 30 and has nothing for Oct 1-2, so check the latest days before changing anything."
